<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The Halo 3-style CARNAGE REPORT (Menu style Halo 3): a multiplayer game's end on every machine
(local, System Link, ad hoc and online; every game type, teams or not), over the game once its
scores come up, in the place of the game's own report (game_engine.c
game_engine_post_rasterize_post_game, drawn by the game with Menu style Halo CE). Built into each
level's map (ingame.txt): pause.xml's fonts and pictures, forge.xml's L and R and its question's
panel. The result in the title strip's line (the winning team or player), the players ranked as the
game ranks them - a team game's under their team's row (its score, its players' sums), the winning
team first -, each on a nameplate in their colour (their team's), this machine's players' rows lit
and the winners' marked. Two pages, L and R (or left and right): SUMMARY (the game type's score -
kills, flags, the ball's or the hill's time, laps -, kills, deaths, assists, kills less deaths)
and DETAILS (suicides, betrayals in a team game, the game type's own: flag grabs and returns, the
ball's kills, the best lap; kills for each death). Up and down scroll a long list. Cross goes on
to the lobby for the game's host (everyone with it, as the host's A on the game's own report), and
by itself after a while; on a machine that joined it waits for the host, and Circle leaves the
game (asked first). Triangle: PLAYERS (players.xml). All the numbers are the game's own record, a
joined machine's the host's (port/linux/game/carnage_report.c); menu_functions.c "port h3 carnage
...". The art is this folder's own (tools/halo3_menu_art.py). -->
